  "id": "pure-tone-audiometry",
  "term": "pure-tone audiometry",
  "definition": "Pure-tone audiometry is the standard hearing test used to measure hearing loss by assessing hearing at specific sound frequencies. In this context, hearing loss may be summarized as a pure-tone average across frequencies such as 0.5, 1, 2, and 4 kHz.",
